# MCP Server Environment Variables
# 
# IMPORTANT: Add these to your shell profile (~/.zshrc, ~/.bashrc, etc.)
# NOT to a .env file, since Claude Code needs them in the shell environment
#
# Example for ~/.zshrc:
#   export YOUR_API_KEY="your_actual_key_here"
#
# After adding, restart your terminal and launch Claude Code from terminal

# Example API keys for MCP servers that require authentication
# GitHub Copilot (if using)
# GITHUB_TOKEN=your_github_token_here

# Add other API keys as needed for your MCP servers

# Looker MCP Server (Google MCP Toolbox for Databases)
# Get credentials from: https://cloud.google.com/looker/docs/api-auth#authentication_with_an_sdk
# LOOKER_BASE_URL=https://looker.example.com
# LOOKER_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id_here
# LOOKER_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret_here
